#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Rating-gap / expected-score / K-RD decomposition of the Lichess kindness surface.

WHY THIS EXISTS
---------------
The certified 24-month surface revealed that raw kindness is not monotone in
chooser draw payoff. Within board-evaluation bands it is often lowest near the
equal-rating/reference neighborhood and rises on both sides, with the positive
draw-payoff / higher-rated-opponent arm typically higher.

This diagnostic asks whether that asymmetric U is:

  A. a genuine function of DISPLAYED RATING DISTANCE;
  B. better organized by Glicko EXPECTED-SCORE DISTANCE;
  C. mechanically generated by the Glicko UPDATE SCALE (the K/RD component);
  D. driven by chooser composition rather than within-chooser behavior;
  E. sensitive to early games (<=10 plies).

The analysis uses ONLY the certified 24-month Stage 07 opportunity panel and
does not modify any canonical source data.

DATA AUTHORITY
--------------
/Volumes/XT_Pro/lichess_kindness/derived/replication/analysis_panel_24m_sf100k
Expected rows: 47,587,020
Expected months: 2023-11 through 2025-10
All observations precede the November 2025 color-advantage production change.

KEY DERIVED OBJECTS
-------------------
Displayed rating gap:
    disconnected_elo - chooser_elo
Positive => disconnected opponent is higher rated.

Opponent-RD discounted expected score (chooser perspective):
    g(phi_j) = 1 / sqrt(1 + 3 phi_j^2 / pi^2)
    E_i      = 1 / [1 + exp{-g(phi_j)(mu_i - mu_j)}]

Expected-score distance:
    |E_i - 0.5|

Effective one-game Glicko update scale K:
    v^{-1}      = g(phi_j)^2 E_i (1-E_i)
    phi_post^2  = 1 / [1/phi_i^2 + v^{-1}]
    K           = 173.7178 * phi_post^2 * g(phi_j)

Under the project's no-same-game-volatility/no-regulator draw construction:
    predicted draw payoff = K * (0.5 - E_i)

The script audits this identity against chooser_draw_payoff_v2 rather than
assuming it.

OUTPUT FAMILIES
---------------
1. mechanical_validation.csv
2. rating_gap_broad_rates.csv
3. rating_gap_u_metrics.csv
4. rating_gap_curves.csv
5. expected_score_curves.csv
6. krd_descriptives.csv
7. fe_model_coefficients.csv
8. fe_model_band_contrasts.csv
9. fe_model_receipts.csv
10. settings.json

FIXED-EFFECTS MODELS
--------------------
Linear probability models with chooser fixed effects, chooser-clustered CR1 SEs.

Within each of five board-evaluation bands and each of:
    all games
    <=10 plies
    >10 plies

GAP model:
  higher-rated-opponent indicator
  absolute displayed rating gap
  absolute gap squared
  higher x absolute gap
  higher x absolute gap squared
  log K
  forgone-win premium
  within-band board-evaluation linear/quadratic terms
  flexible ply-band controls

SCORE model:
  analogous model replacing rating distance by expected-score distance.

HORSE-RACE model:
  rating distance and expected-score distance together plus log K.
  To limit redundant computation, this is run for ALL and >10-ply games in
  the three nonnegative/competitive board-state bands.

The point is diagnostic decomposition, not structural utility estimation.
"""

